  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It can often be helpful to use custom components to help with constructing worlds and avatars. However, If a world or avatar is uploaded with a custom component, this results in a bunch of logspam on load, which is a bit unfortunate, and is presumably why the VRCSDK disallows custom components on avatars.\nYou can, of course, use SDK build pipeline hooks to strip custom components at build time, and use reflection to then allow those components to be included on an avatar upload. But it would be better to have a well-supported mechanism that ensures that these components don't leak into the built asset bundle, while also allowing them to be present at the start of the upload process.\nTherefore, I'd request the creation of a `EditorComponent` abstract class in the SDK, extending from `MonoBehavior`. This class (and subclasses) would get the following special treatment:\n1. For the purposes of SDK warnings and pre-upload checks, the component is treated as being whitelisted.\n2. Just before the asset bundle/prefab is generated, all EditorComponents are destroyed.\nBy extending this EditorComponent class, we can add custom components to avatars and worlds without triggering SDK warnings, and without creating logspam in the client, in a standardized way that avoids the risk of someone forgetting to strip the components at build.",
